      "proposition": {
        "predicate": "summary",
        "object": "<p>Recent strikes have sent oil prices climbing again, with average gas price per gallon up by $0.70 compared with 2025</p><p>Inflation cooled to an annual rate of 3.5% in June as the brief US-Iran ceasefire, which has since ended, brought energy prices down, according to new data from the Bureau of Labor Statistics.</p><p>The consumer price index (CPI), which measures a basket of goods and services, has been elevated since the start of the war, largely because of higher energy prices. After mostly staying under 3% since mid-2024, CPI reached a three-year high of 4.2% in May – up from 2.4% in February. Month-over-month, CPI fell 0.8% in June, the largest one-month decrease since April 2020.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/jul/14/june-cpi-report-inflation-cools-iran-deal\">Continue reading...</a>"
